+++ b/LOCAL-MODEL-STAGING.md
@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@
+# Selected-file local staging
+
+The candidate chart adds opt-in localModel staging without changing the default
+model-serving configuration. It is intended for large immutable lookup tables,
+not full-checkpoint prefetch.
+
+When enabled, supply a source PVC, an exact preparation receipt, a revision,
+and a filename/size/SHA256 manifest. An init container mounts that PVC read-only,
+checks its receipt and current local free space, and copies only selected files
+to a disk-backed emptyDir. It checks input hashes and independently rehashes
+destination files before an atomic rename. Source and destination cache pages
+are advised away during copying/verification.
+
+The engine mounts /local-model read-only and never mounts the source PVC.
+The disk volume has no medium: Memory. Staging requires an engine ephemeral-storage
+request and limit; reserve the local volume plus normal temporary/log overhead.
+The stage init is CPU-only and uses at most 512 MiB by container limit; flushing
+and dropping cache every 32 MiB bounds copying's dirty-page window.
+
+Completed copies survive a container restart in the same pod and are rehashed
+if the init runs again. They disappear with the pod. Keep the source PVC.
+Neither a sizeLimit nor a scheduler request preallocates local disk; check current
+free space and node pressure before activation. Buffer/cache and memory safety
+still require real observation.
+
+Offline checks:
+
+```sh
+python3 -m unittest discover -s checks -v
+helm lint charts/pcai-inference
+```
+
+The initial EAQ candidate uses two original Engram shards (~189.13 GiB) and their
+index, a 230 GiB local volume, 32 GiB free-space headroom, and a 240/260 GiB
+engine ephemeral-storage request/limit. The staging addition does not itself
+make EXL3 or a disk Engram runtime available; use a separately qualified image.
